Q: How do I set a page&#39;s base href in Javascript? A: <p>I think you'd better do it this way</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
        document.head.innerHTML = document.head.innerHTML + &quot;&lt;base href='&quot; + document.location.href + &quot;' /&gt;&quot;;
    &lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>As <code>location.hostname</code> does not return the application context root! You could also log the <code>document.location</code> on the console <code>console.log</code> to see all available metadata on <code>document.location</code>.</p>
